exports[`a project with access on databricks > says in its passport who may use it, and what is enforced where 1`] = `
"## Who may use it

### customers

#### \`dev.bronze.customers\`

| Role | Principal in dev | Access | Purpose | Approvers | Granted |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| marketing-analysts | marketing-analysts-dev | read | Campaign reporting | mia@example.com | Granted on Databricks. |
| crm-loaders | crm-loaders | write |  |  | Granted on Databricks. |
| data-engineers | data-engineers | write |  |  | Granted on Databricks. |

Grant mode: exact. On Databricks, any other access granted directly on the table is taken away, except the owner's, the run_as principal's and the unmasked principals'; grants on its schema or catalog stay.

Masked columns:

- \`email\` (confidential): hashed, on Databricks.

Row filters:

- \`region_rows\`: \`region_filter\` decides which rows each reader sees, from \`country\`, on Databricks.
"
`;

